  "name": "schliff",
  "description": "Deterministic linter and scorer for instruction files — SKILL.md, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md. No model in the loop: the same bytes score the same everywhere. Use for linting, scoring, auditing or CI-gating an instruction file, and for checking whether the commands a file promises actually resolve in the repo. Trigger phrases: \"lint my skill\", \"score my skill\", \"audit skill\", \"review my skill\", \"harden skill\", \"make this skill better\", \"optimize my skill\", \"improve [metric] from X to Y\", \"benchmark skill\", \"check my AGENTS.md\", \"is my AGENTS.md lying\", or paste a SKILL.md for auto-analysis. Also use when a user shares an instruction file without explicit instructions. Do NOT use for authoring a file from scratch — use a skill-creator first, then schliff. Do NOT use for application-code linting, SQL tuning, or runtime behaviour testing.",
